<title>SINGAPORE: Four directors of Kay Hian resign.</title>
<headline>Four directors of Kay Hian resign.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage Kay Hian Holdings Ltd said on Monday four of its directors would be resigning with effect from February 1, 1997.</p>
<p>They were Philip John Scott Gray, Ip Siok Hui, Lim Ah Swan and Christopher Chong Meng Tak.</p>
<p>Last year, James Capel said it would substantially reduce its stake in the brokerage company. James Capel now holds four percent stake in Kay Hian.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703083)</p>
